STEP 3: The cycle that doesn't bound
========================================================================

  The 1-cycle in β₁=1 tournament that has no 2-chain boundary:
    +1·(0→5)
    +1·(1→0)
    +1·(5→1)
  Total: 3 edges in the cycle

  This cycle exists in ker(∂₁) but NOT in im(∂₂).
  It wraps around the tournament in a way that no combination
  of transitive triples can decompose.

